From ca02d8d9ad90a0a1afdfe826949b82d4762ac3bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "crychic.tan" <crychic.tan@cybertan.com.tw>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:49:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: mtk_ppe: read the last counters of unbound flows

When a PPE flow entry is no longer bound, its last counters are taken
from the value read at the previous stats update instead of the MIB
table, so what the hardware counted since then is lost. With the flower
stats polled once per second, bridged uplink TCP transfers of 1 s from a
station were counted at 61 % on average, which feeds wrong packet counts
into bridger.

Add a target patch that reads the MIB counters once more when the entry
has left the bind state.

Signed-off-by: crychic.tan <crychic.tan@cybertan.com.tw>
---
 ...d-the-last-counters-of-unbound-flows.patch | 45 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 45 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/999-2703-net-ethernet-mtk_ppe-read-the-last-counters-of-unbound-flows.patch

diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/999-2703-net-ethernet-mtk_ppe-read-the-last-counters-of-unbound-flows.patch b/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/999-2703-net-ethernet-mtk_ppe-read-the-last-counters-of-unbound-flows.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..3b4bed45af
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/999-2703-net-ethernet-mtk_ppe-read-the-last-counters-of-unbound-flows.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+From: crychic.tan <crychic.tan@cybertan.com.tw>
+Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_ppe: read the last counters of unbound flows
+
+Since "net: ethernet: mediatek: fix ppe flow accounting for L2 flows",
+the counters of a flow are read from the MIB table while its hardware
+entry is bound, and once the entry is no longer bound the last value is
+added to prev_packets/prev_bytes. That value is the one read at the
+previous update though. The MIB counters are read-clear, so whatever the
+hardware counted between that update and the end of the flow is never
+read, and for an L2 subflow it is lost for good, as the subflow is freed
+right after.
+
+An entry that forwards a TCP FIN goes to FIN state and is aged out one
+second later, so with the stats polled once per second the end of such a
+connection is usually missed, and a connection shorter than that is often
+not counted at all. On MT7981, bridged uplink TCP transfers from a station
+(WED rx) of 1 s were counted at 7-111 % (61 % on average) of the bytes
+received, and 3 s transfers at 70-104 %.
+
+__mtk_ppe_check_skb() drops the flows of a hash bucket before it binds
+another flow to one of its entries, so the counters left in the MIB table
+still belong to this flow. Read them once more instead of using the
+cached value. With this, the same 1 s and 3 s transfers are counted at
+105-115 % (the PPE counts L2 frames), like downlink transfers.
+
+Signed-off-by: crychic.tan <crychic.tan@cybertan.com.tw>
+---
+ drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c |    6 +++++-
+ 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
++++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
+@@ -584,7 +584,11 @@ mtk_flow_entry_update(struct mtk_ppe *pp
+ 
+ 	if (!mtk_flow_entry_match(ppe->eth, entry, &foe, len) ||
+ 	    FIELD_GET(MTK_FOE_IB1_STATE, foe.ib1) != MTK_FOE_STATE_BIND) {
+-		acct = mtk_ppe_acct_data(ppe, hash);
++		/* No other flow has been bound to this entry since this one,
++		 * so what the hardware counted after the last update belongs
++		 * to this flow: read the counters once more.
++		 */
++		acct = mtk_ppe_mib_entry_read(ppe, hash);
+ 		if (acct) {
+ 			entry->prev_packets += acct->packets;
+ 			entry->prev_bytes += acct->bytes;
-- 
